.TH I-NIX 1 "2026-09-26" "i-nix 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
i-nix \- imperative UX for declarative Nix/NixOS systems
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B i-nix
[\fB\-c\fR \fICONFIG\-DIR\fR] [\fB\-n\fR] [\fB\-v\fR] [\fBCOMMAND\fR] [\fIARGS\fR...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B i-nix
is a UX layer that compiles imperative commands into declarative NixOS/Home Manager configuration. It is inspired by the workflow of
.B nh
(Yet Another Nix Helper) but implemented natively in Rust with zero external dependencies.
.PP
Every action you take becomes part of a clean, reproducible Nix configuration stored in
.IR ~/.config/i-nix/flake/ .
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-config\-dir " " \fIDIR\fR
Path to the i-nix configuration directory. Defaults to
.IR ~/.config/i-nix .
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-dry\-run
Show what would be done without doing it.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Be verbose about what is happening.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print help.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print version.
.SH COMMANDS
.SS Core Commands
.TP
.BR init " [\fB\-\-hostname\fR \fIHOST\fR] [\fB\-\-user\fR|\fB\-\-system\fR]"
Initialize a new i-nix flake.
.TP
.BR install " \fIPACKAGE\fR... [\fB\-\-user\fR] [\fB\-\-program\fR]"
Install packages declaratively.
.TP
.BR remove " \fIPACKAGE\fR... [\fB\-\-user\fR]"
Remove packages from configuration.
.TP
.BR list " [\fB\-\-user\fR|\fB\-\-system\fR]"
List declaratively managed packages.
.TP
.BR search " \fIQUERY\fR [\fB\-\-limit\fR \fIN\fR] [\fB\-\-json\fR]"
Search nixpkgs.
.SS Services and Programs
.TP
.BR enable " \fISERVICE\fR|\fIPROGRAM\fR [\fB\-\-user\fR] [\fB\-\-program\fR]"
Enable a service or program.
.TP
.BR disable " \fISERVICE\fR|\fIPROGRAM\fR [\fB\-\-user\fR]"
Disable a service or program.
.SS NixOS Operations (nh os)
.TP
.BR os " \fISUBCOMMAND\fR [\fB\-H\fR \fIHOSTNAME\fR]"
NixOS system operations.
.RS
.TP
.B switch
Build and activate the new configuration, and make it the boot default.
.TP
.B boot
Build the new configuration and make it the boot default.
.TP
.B test
Build and activate the new configuration.
.TP
.B build
Build the new configuration.
.TP
.B info
List available generations from profile path.
.TP
.B repl
Load system configuration in a Nix REPL.
.RE
.SS Home Manager Operations (nh home)
.TP
.BR home " \fISUBCOMMAND\fR [\fB\-u\fR \fIUSER\fR] [\fB\-H\fR \fIHOSTNAME\fR]"
Home-manager operations.
.RS
.TP
.B switch
Build and activate a home-manager configuration.
.TP
.B build
Build a home-manager configuration.
.TP
.B repl
Load a home-manager configuration in a Nix REPL.
.RE
.SS Cleanup (nh clean)
.TP
.BR clean " \fISUBCOMMAND\fR"
Enhanced nix cleanup.
.RS
.TP
.B all
Clean all profiles.
.TP
.B user
Clean the current user's profiles.
.TP
.B profile
Clean a specific profile.
.RE
.SS Desktop Environment
.TP
.BR desktop " \fISUBCOMMAND\fR"
Manage desktop environments.
.RS
.TP
.B detect
Auto-detect the current desktop environment.
.TP
.B list
List all supported desktop environments.
.TP
.B generate " \fIDE\fR"
Generate declarative configuration for a desktop environment.
.TP
.B apply
Wire the generated desktop configuration into the flake.
.RE
.SS Other Commands
.TP
.BR diff
Show pending changes.
.TP
.BR apply " [\fB\-\-test\fR] [\fB\-\-remote\fR \fIHOST\fR]"
Evaluate, build, and switch.
.TP
.BR rollback " [\fB\-i\fR|\fB\-g\fR \fIGEN\fR]"
Rollback to a previous generation.
.TP
.BR update
Update flake inputs.
.TP
.BR edit " [\fBpackages\fR|\fBservices\fR|\fBprograms\fR]"
Open configuration in $EDITOR.
.TP
.BR why " \fIPACKAGE\fR"
Show dependency chain.
.TP
.BR adopt " [\fB\-\-write\fR]"
Discover current system state.
.TP
.BR doctor
Diagnose Nix/NixOS health.
.TP
.BR sync " [\fB\-\-yes\fR]"
Detect and re-import changes.
.TP
.BR shell " [\fIPACKAGE\fR...] [\fB\-\-flake\fR] [\fB\-\-list\fR]"
Start a development shell.
.TP
.BR dev " [\fISTACK\fR] [\fINAME\fR] [\fB\-\-list\fR]"
Scaffold a new Nix development project.
.TP
.BR container " \fIACTION\fR [\fITARGET\fR]"
Build and manage OCI container images.
.TP
.BR tui
Launch the interactive terminal UI.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/i-nix/
Configuration directory.
.TP
.I ~/.config/i-nix/flake/
Generated Nix flake.
.TP
.I ~/.config/i-nix/flake/flake.nix
Main flake file.
.TP
.I ~/.config/i-nix/flake/hosts/default.nix
Multi-host registry.
.TP
.I ~/.config/i-nix/flake/systems/
System configurations.
.TP
.I ~/.config/i-nix/flake/users/
User configurations.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B EDITOR
Text editor used by the
.B edit
command.
.TP
.B HOME
User's home directory.
.TP
.B USER
Current username.
.SH EXAMPLES
Initialize a new system configuration:
.PP
.nf
.RS
i-nix init --hostname laptop --system
.RE
.fi
.PP
Install packages:
.PP
.nf
.RS
i-nix install firefox git vim
i-nix install --user kitty neovim
.RE
.fi
.PP
Enable a service:
.PP
.nf
.RS
i-nix enable ssh
i-nix enable --user kitty
.RE
.fi
.PP
Build and switch NixOS configuration:
.PP
.nf
.RS
i-nix os switch --hostname laptop
.RE
.fi
.PP
Build and switch Home Manager configuration:
.PP
.nf
.RS
i-nix home switch --user lin --hostname laptop
.RE
.fi
.PP
Clean up old generations:
.PP
.nf
.RS
i-nix clean all
.RE
.fi
.PP
Generate GNOME desktop configuration:
.PP
.nf
.RS
i-nix desktop generate gnome
i-nix desktop apply
.RE
.fi
.PP
Rollback to a specific generation:
.PP
.nf
.RS
i-nix rollback -g 42
.RE
.fi
.PP
Run via nix:
.PP
.nf
.RS
nix run github:stefan-hacks/i-nix -- --help
.RE
.fi
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
General error.
.TP
.B 2
Configuration error.
.TP
.B 3
Build error.
